      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "4.1",
      "title": "Historical Sources and Datation",
      "body": "Type 1 falchions are based on Elmslie typology. They are characterized by a flaring profile, and broad, abrupt tip.\nThere are 4 subtypes, from 1a to 1d.\nAll subtypes type 1 falchion have been used since the 13th century.\nThey are Approved for 14th century, Transitional and 15th century armors.\nType 1d falchion is Denied because its pointy edge is not safe.\n\nAPPROVED DENIED\n\nFalchion of Cluny - 1270/1280 - France\n\nFalchion of Conyers - 1260/1270 - England",
