      "depth": 1,
      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "5.1",
      "title": "Historical Sources and Datation",
      "body": "Type 2 falchions are based on Elmslie typology. They are also called “reverse-edge falchions”. They are sharpened along the ‘short’ edge, which features a clipped portion, leading to the reinforced thrusting tip.\nThey are Approved for 14th century, Transitional and 15th century armors.\nA particular attention must be paid to the safety of the pointy edge, it must be made to be safe.\n\nBNF Français 246 Histoire Ancienne - C. 1360-1400 - France\n\nFlemish Falchion - C. 1400 - Musée de L’Armée - France\n\nCastello di Avio - 1350 - Italy",
