    {
      "ordinal": 15,
      "depth": 1,
      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "6.1",
      "title": "Historical Sources and Datation",
      "body": "Type 3 falchions are based on Elmslie typology. They are characterized by having scalloped or cutaway tips on the blades of various shapes. The curvature of the blade can vary.\nThere are 5 subtypes, from 3a to 3e.\nAll type 3 falchions have been used since the 14th century.\nThey are Approved for 14th century, Transitional and 15th century armors.\nA particular attention must be paid to the safety of the pointy edge, it must be made to be safe.\n\nFalchion from Thorpe - 1350 - England\n\nBNF Français 167 Bible Moralisée - 1345/1355 - France\n\nMorgan M.394 Bible Historiale - 1415 - France",
