    {
      "ordinal": 21,
      "depth": 1,
      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "8.1",
      "title": "Historical Sources and Datation",
      "body": "Type 5 falchions are based on Elmslie typology. They are characterized by relatively symmetrical profiles, typically featuring little to no curvature over their length.\nThere are 5 subtypes, from 4a to 4e.\nAll type 5 falchions have been used since the 14th century.\nSubtypes 5a, 5b, 5c falchions are Approved for 14th century, Transitional and 15th century armors.\nSubtypes 5d and 5e are Denied for safety reasons.\n\nAPPROVED\n\nDENIED\n\nMorgan M.394 Bible Historiale - 1415 - France",
      "page_from": 16,
      "page_to": 17,
