    {
      "ordinal": 23,
      "depth": 1,
      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "9.1",
      "title": "Historical Sources and Datation",
      "body": "2-handed falchions are not based on Elmslie typology. They are depicted in manuscripts from the middle ages in Europe.\nThere are 3 subtypes of 2-handed that are suitable for buhurt:\n● Type 2 It has a similar shape to 1-handed falchion type 2, with a square guard.\n● Type 3c It has a similar shape to 1-handed falchion type 3c.\n● Type 3e It has a similar shape to 1-handed falchion type 3e.\n\nThey are Approved for 14th century, Transitional and 15th century armors.\n\n2-handed Type 2\n\nRomance of Alexander - 1338/1344 - England\n\n2-handed Type 3c\n\nLyon BM PA 30 Cy commencent les grans croniques de la genealogie des roys de France - 1380 - France\n\n2-handed Type 3e\n\nMartyr of Saint Savinien - Bibliotheque Nationale de France - Department of Manuscripts 50 f. 324v. - second half of the 14th century - France",
