      "title": "1-Handed Falchions with D-guards",
      "body": "From the 16th century, mainly in Italy, falchions with “D Guard” started to be used for civil combats.\nThey represent a serious risk of injury and can not be used.\n\nAll 1-handed falchions reproducing the designs of a 1-handed falchion with a D-guard are Denied.\n\n1.1. Examples of Denied Reproductions\n\nPicture from Medieval Extreme ©",
